      },
      "excerpt": "Colonel Aaron Burgstein Memorial Scholarship offers one nonrenewable1000award to a minor dependent of active, retired or prior-service personnel, Reserve or National Guard in any branch, accepted or enrolling in an accredited two- or four-year degree. GPA must be2.5–4.0 without rounding. Priority applies when a parent/guardian served eight or more years, died on active duty or is classified through Air Force Wounded Warrior; these are priorities, not universal requirements. Selection considers academics, character, commitment to others and goals. Submit a600-word essay, non-family/non-friend recommendation, official transcript, acceptance/enrollment and service verification through the provider-linked named SmarterSelect record. Deadline and current opening were not returned; do not assume an open cycle. Recipients must supply aW-9 beforedisbursement;no suchmaterialaccessed.",
