      "excerpt": "Gold Memorial Scholarship provides20000in four annual5000installments to a female graduating high-school senior who is the daughter/dependent of a currently serving, retired or deceased Air Force member, excelled in mathematics, and is accepted at an accredited four-year institution for a STEM bachelor degree. FAFSA-documented financial need is a preference, not a universal eligibility condition. Continued installments require transcript proof of STEM enrollment and a sponsor update letter. The introduction expands STEM with Education, but the explicit eligibility list says Engineering; apply the specific list and do not include all education majors. The named SmarterSelect record is provider-linked. NumericGPA, deadline and current opening were not returned. Recipients must supply aW-9 beforedisbursement;no suchmaterialaccessed.",
